# After a failed header CRC the receiver takes the packet's data for a packet (the data is a header's image), with neither the wait for 528 zeros nor the mask on the data. Either of the two is enough here
# found by linksearch --rules hl-flush-mask
sizes number_bits=3 max_words=1 window=2 zeros=40 flush_zeros=32 status_timer=24 queue=8 reask=96 pass=1 restart_words=1 delay=1 words=1 images=1 window0=0 wrong=0 still=0
packets 1 0 1 0
offer 0 1 216
fate 1 4 first0
offer 1 1 217
fate 0 5 header
quiet 234 20000
run hl-flush-mask fail the link started again, and nothing had happened that could excuse it
run hl-flush ok
run hl-mask ok
run hl ok
